          "message": "fix(velvet)!: resolve Tailwind v4's flex shorthand utilities and give flex-1 its 0% basis (#1401)\n\n## What & why\n\n`flex-<N>`, `flex-<a>/<b>` and `flex-[…]` were left in the class list and resolved nothing. They now parse to the three flex longhands (`ArbitraryProperty.Flex`), and `grow-*`, `shrink-*` and `basis-*` beside one take their own part whichever is listed first, as Tailwind declares the shorthand ahead of them. Against a class of the same property they are ordered by `StyleRuleOrder`, as every other inline token is.\n\n- `flex-1` gets the `0%` basis Tailwind's `flex: 1` has, where it had `0px`. A `flex-1` child of a column that sizes to its content keeps its content height. This is the breaking part.\n- A basis the element measures (`2em`, `50vw`, `calc(…)`) is carried as an expression.\n- `border-t-0`, `border-r-0`, `border-b-0`, `border-l-0`, `border-x-0` and `border-y-0` ship in `_borders.uss`, as Tailwind does. The generator census follows (`SurveyedRuleCount` 2241, single-class 2203, utility classes 2151); the committed `StyleUtilityProperties.g.cs` matches a fresh derivation.\n- `origin/main` is merged in. `StyleInlineSheetOrder`'s rewrite is kept, and the one call the branch renames (`IsSpacingRadiusOrFlexProperty`) is renamed there too. The ordering cases (`flex-none flex-2`, `flex-1 flex-0`, `flex-2 flex-1`) hold under main's order key: the candidate-name tiebreak puts `flex-0` before `flex-1` before `flex-2` before `flex-none`.\n- `FlexShorthandTests` asserts one fact per case, over table rows.\n- The label-swap comment in `FiberNodePatcher` now says which transition a swap plays on, which the code resolves in `ResolvePlayedSwap`; it did not say so before.\n\nRefs #1118\n\n**Docs:** `styling-flexbox-and-gap.md` and the `Documentation~/README.md` row. **Changelog:** a `breaking` and an `unreleased` fragment named for the branch.\n\n**Verification:** generator suite 498 passed, 1 failed (`GeneratorProjectOptInDriftTests`, which needs the pinned SDK 10.0.103 that is not installed here). The Unity suites were not run locally; `Test ▸ unity-tests` and `Test ▸ base-red` take them. `mutation_check.py --list` reports 61 mutants over the change.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [ ] Tests pass locally (EditMode / PlayMode / generator tests as applicable) — generator suite run locally; Unity suites run in CI only\n- [ ] New regression tests were verified red without the change and green with it — left to `Test ▸ base-red` and `Test ▸ unity-tests`\n- [x] Docs are updated for every fact this change touches (guides, READMEs, CLAUDE.md) — or this PR has no doc impact\n- [x] CHANGELOG fragment added for behavior/perf changes, named for the branch with `/` as `-` — inline under `## [Unreleased]` on a maintenance line with no `scripts/release/compile_changelog.py` (pure refactors are omitted by convention)\n- [x] Known gaps or deliberate deferrals discovered here are filed as issues with acceptance criteria — none outstanding\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01FoK7YxdRjMGmfmRkEEmS88)_",
