          "distinct": true,
          "id": "533d1e78768082f4b0def2b0ab4ce1aecf66e3c4",
          "message": "fix(velvet): run a layoutId crossfade's own opacity on the transition UI Toolkit is running (#1406)\n\n## What & why\n\nRefs #1116\n\nThe first of four stacked changes bringing a layoutId lead's shared-layout look in line with Framer Motion's\n`mixValues` and `NodeStack.promote`. Branch `fix/1116-layoutid-tail-ported-1` is cut from `main`; the next three\n(`-2`, `-3`, `-4`) each build on the one before.\n\n**An opacity transition already running as a crossfade starts is taken over, not restarted.** While a crossfade\ndraws an element's opacity, the element's own opacity is carried on the transition its classes declare for it. When\nUI Toolkit is already running such a transition on the element as the crossfade first draws it, the carry now\ncontinues that transition: from where the engine had got, over the time the engine has left including a delay not\nyet served, on the engine's own easing curve. A change of the element's own opacity back towards the value the\nrunning transition started from runs over a duration shortened by how far the transition had got, as the engine\nshortens a reversing transition. Where the panel's running transitions cannot be read, the carry starts from where\nthe element stands, as it did. This replaces the previous reaction to the engine's transition-cancel event, which\ncarried what was left of the duration with none of its delay and could not shorten a reversal; that callback and\nits registration are gone.\n\n**A lead whose own move interrupts a shared move keeps what the shared move had reached.** A lead alone under its\nid whose own move starts while its opacity mix from the previous holder runs keeps drawing the opacity the mix had\nreached until that move lands, whatever happens meanwhile to its own opacity classes or to the holder it took its\nbox from. A member drawn fading out behind a lead whose own move interrupts the crossfade keeps the fade it had\nreached in the same way. Framer renders `lead.animationValues || lead.latestValues`, and `promote` hands the next\nlead the previous lead's `animationValues`, so the values a stopped animation left stay what is drawn.\n\n**Engine reads.** `EngineMember` declares the animation-system members the take-over reads (the panel's running\ntransitions per value type, their timing and their start, end and reversing values), and its shapes can name a\ngeneric definition's own type parameter (`generic:T`), since those members are declared on generic types.\n`RunningStyleTransition` reads them; a member that does not resolve leaves the take-over undone.\n\n## Documentation, changelog and tests\n\n- `motion.md` describes the take-over and the hold in the crossfade paragraph; `player-builds.md` lists the new\n  engine reads and the generic-definition shape rule.\n- Changelog fragment `fix-1116-layoutid-tail-ported-1.md` (user-visible behaviour).\n- New cases: three for the hold, three for the take-over (inside a delay, a negative delay, a reversal), and two for\n  the generic-parameter shape; the one that keeps a same-named class out of that shape passes on the base and is\n  declared `GREEN_ON_BASE`. The ownership cases that pinned the cancel-event callback are removed with it.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [ ] Tests pass locally (EditMode / PlayMode / generator tests as applicable)\n- [ ] New regression tests were verified red without the change and green with it\n- [x] Docs are updated for every fact this change touches (guides, READMEs, CLAUDE.md) — or this PR has no doc impact\n- [x] CHANGELOG fragment added for behavior/perf changes, named for the branch with `/` as `-` — inline under `## [Unreleased]` on a maintenance line with no `scripts/release/compile_changelog.py` (pure refactors are omitted by convention)\n- [ ] Known gaps or deliberate deferrals discovered here are filed as issues with acceptance criteria\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01FoK7YxdRjMGmfmRkEEmS88)_",
