          "message": "fix(velvet)!: scale a caret colour's alpha by its modifier and read bracket units, math spacing and angles as CSS does (#1404)\n\n## What & why\n\nPart 1 of a stack that splits a branch too large to review in one pull request. Each part is built on `main`\nor on the part before it, compiles alone and carries its own tests.\n\n- `caret-*`, `selection:bg-*` and `selection:text-*` read their colour through a parser that wrote an opacity\n  modifier's N% as the alpha, where `bg-`, `text-` and `border-` multiply the colour's own alpha by it, as\n  Tailwind's `color-mix` with `transparent` does. They now read the parser `bg-` reads, as a colour longhand\n  (so `hsl()` saturation keeps clamping), and the parser they used is removed.\n- A bracketed length's unit is read in any case, as CSS reads it (`w-[10PX]`), except where Tailwind reads a\n  bracket as a length or a colour and its length test is case-sensitive.\n- An angle or a time unit is read in any case (`rotate-[45DEG]`, `duration-[150MS]`), and a bracket the browser\n  rejects (`rotate-[45]`, `rotate-[0]`, a bare non-zero gradient angle, `bg-conic-[45deg]`) is declined. The\n  breaking changelog fragment records that.\n- A math function is spaced as Tailwind's `addWhitespaceAroundMathOperators` spaces it, and its name is read\n  in any case.\n- `TryParseBracketValue` and `TailwindMathSpacing.Format` are split so that no member makes more than the twenty\n  branching decisions VEL501 allows; no behaviour changes.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [ ] Tests pass locally (EditMode / PlayMode / generator tests as applicable) — not run here: no Unity editor was available; `Test ▸ unity-tests` and `Test ▸ base-red` are what measure them\n- [ ] New regression tests were verified red without the change and green with it — left to `Test ▸ base-red`; the cases that are green on the base carry a `GREEN_ON_BASE` declaration\n- [x] Docs are updated for every fact this change touches (`styling-arbitrary-lengths.md`, `styling-colors.md`, `styling-gradients.md`)\n- [x] CHANGELOG fragment added for behavior/perf changes, named for the branch with `/` as `-` (`unreleased/` and `breaking/`)\n- [x] Known gaps or deliberate deferrals discovered here are filed as issues with acceptance criteria — none found\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01FoK7YxdRjMGmfmRkEEmS88)_",
