          "distinct": true,
          "id": "0c7940bccae36c847299ca8725b4d6820a2cd9fa",
          "message": "fix(velvet)!: draw shadow-* as Tailwind v4's box-shadow layers, shear it on both axes and draw inset shadows (#1430)\n\n## What & why\n\n`shadow-*` was one soft tinted glow on Velvet's own scale, drawn from a single blur and sheared on the x axis only. It now follows CSS `box-shadow` and Tailwind v4:\n\n- `shadow-*` presets are Tailwind v4's, layers and all: `shadow-lg` is `0 10px 15px -3px` and `0 4px 6px -4px`, both black at 10%. `shadow-2xs` and `shadow-xs` are added.\n- Each layer is drawn as CSS draws it: the spread grows or shrinks the box with CSS's corner-radius rule, the blur is a Gaussian of half the blur radius, nothing is drawn inside the element's border box, and the first layer is on top. A translucent background no longer shows the shadow through it.\n- `shadow-[...]` takes a comma-separated list of shadows and rejects a negative blur. Each corner of the shadow follows its own corner of the element, where all four followed the top-left one.\n- `shadow-inner` and an `inset` layer in `shadow-[...]` draw an inner shadow inside the padding box.\n- A `shadow-*` on a `skew-y-*` element follows the y shear as well as the x one, composed as Tailwind's `skewX() skewY()` transform. Its offset shears with the element, and a steep skew no longer cuts the shadow off at the edge of the area it is painted into.\n- An element with both `skew-x-*` and `skew-y-*` is sheared as that product for its face, bounds, gradient fill and children's seating too; they used the simultaneous matrix `[[1, tanX], [tanY, 1]]`, which left the shadow and the face about `tanX·tanY·w/2` apart at the sides and is singular where `tanX·tanY` is 1.\n- A shadow layer is drawn at its real size: the quad was clamped to 8..2048px per side, which stretched an inset layer on an element under 8px past it.\n- Unsupported and stated in the guide: `shadow-<color>`, `shadow-lg/50`, `shadow-[#f00]`, `inset-shadow-*`, and elliptical padding-box radii.\n\nThe change is breaking for an application that relied on the old preset look, so its fragment is `Changelog~/breaking/fix-1120-drop-shadow-ported-3.md`.\n\nStacked on the squash-merged `-2` (#1413); this branch carries main merged in, and its own diff against main is the single commit `fb22cc08`.\n\nRefs #1120\n\n## Tests\n\n- Reworked or added: `BoxShadowBakeTests` (Gaussian falloff, box cut-out, spread and per-corner radius, inset band and padding box, shear overhang), `ShadowClassParityTests` (v4 preset layers, lists, inset, negative blur), `SilhouetteBoundsSpacerTests` (sheared on both axes), `PaintBindingPatchTests`, `VariantGateTokenPriorityTests`, and the PlayMode `ShaderBackedPaintRuntimeTests` (y-skewed caster tilts the way the face does).\n- Added: both-axes cases for `SilhouetteFace.Shear`, `ShearedAabb`, `ComputeOffset`, the gradient `QuadSize` and the shadow's rect against the face's sheared corners; a `skew-y-3` to `skew-y-6` patch case; a PlayMode thin-inset case. The PlayMode y-skew pair is one case. The both-axes and thin-inset cases cannot show red locally (no editor); `SilhouetteFace.Shear`, `ShearedAabb`, `ComputeOffset` and `QuadSize` exist on the base, so those four are red there by value, and the rest call surface this branch adds.\n- `VariantGateTokenPriorityTests` reads the front layer by name so the fixture builds on the base; ten cases it promotes carry a `GREEN_ON_BASE(refactor)` declaration.\n- Merge resolution: in `ShadowClassParityTests` main's one-value assertion for `shadow-lg` + `drop-shadow-none` was kept; `assume_gate_baseline.txt` was regenerated with `--write-baseline`.\n- Red-on-base evidence comes from `Test > base-red` in CI; the plan lists the cases in scope, two of them declared `[characterization]`. Not run locally: no Unity editor on this machine.\n\n## Docs / CHANGELOG\n\n- Docs: new `Documentation~/styling-shadows.md`, index row in `Documentation~/README.md`, and a one-line fix in `styling-variants.md`.\n- CHANGELOG: breaking fragment `Changelog~/breaking/fix-1120-drop-shadow-ported-3.md`.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01FoK7YxdRjMGmfmRkEEmS88)_",
