          "distinct": true,
          "id": "e28fec06be232f629983c1b9424acf33313e990d",
          "message": "fix(velvet)!: read Tailwind's bracket type hints, and draw ring and outline with Tailwind v4's defaults (#1429)\n\n## What & why\n\nPart 3 of a stack that splits a branch too large to review in one pull request. Parts 1 and 2 are on `main` as #1404 and #1418, and this part is built on `main`.\n\n**Type hints.** Tailwind reads `[length:…]`, `[color:…]` and the like at the start of a bracket as a type hint. Velvet read only `text-[length:…]`. A bracket utility the resolver parses now drops the hint (`w-[length:10px]` is `w-[10px]`, `gap-[length:8px]` is `gap-[8px]`, `rotate-[angle:45deg]` is `rotate-[45deg]`), and an empty hint (`w-[:10px]`) is none. The utilities that infer length or colour from the value (`border-*`, `text-*`, `outline-*`, `ring-*`, `ring-offset-*`, `from-*` / `via-*` / `to-*`) take the branch the hint names in place of their tests (`text-*` also takes `size`), and any other hint selects the colour, so `border-[length:2PX]` is 2px, `text-[color:#f00]` a colour and `bg-[color:#f00]/50` a half-transparent red. A hint with no value after it leaves the class inert. `drop-shadow-*` and `font-[…]` take no hint. `filter-[name:args]` and `bg-[addr:key]` are Velvet's own colon forms and are not read as hints. `text-[length:red]` is no longer a colour, which is a fix to the base behaviour.\n\n**Ring and outline defaults.** Ring and outline are drawn with Tailwind v4's defaults: `ring` is 1px where it was 3px, a band naming no colour is drawn in the element's text colour (following it as it changes) where it was blue-500, a colour class alone (`ring-red-500`) draws nothing, and a ring colour no longer colours an outline.\n\n**`grid-cols-[…]`.** A bracket is read as the track list Tailwind writes: `grid-cols-[repeat(5,minmax(0,1fr))]` is five columns, while `grid-cols-[5]` is a declaration the browser rejects and leaves the class inert.\n\nThe ring, outline and `grid-cols-[…]` changes are in the breaking changelog fragment.\n\n## Tests\n\n- `TypeHintTests` is new and holds one case per utility family the hint reaches, with controls for the unhinted spelling and for a hint naming the other branch.\n- `StyleRingClassTests`, `RingOverlayTests` and `ClipPathWrapTests` pin the v4 defaults, one fact per case; `RingSpecReader` holds the reflection read of `RingSpec.CurrentColor` in its own file so `StyleRingClassTests` has no changed line outside a case.\n- `GridParityTests` replaces the bare-bracket column count case with the declined bare bracket and the track-list form.\n- Not run here: no Unity editor was available. `Test ▸ unity-tests` and `Test ▸ base-red` measure them; `base_red_check.py --plan` names the changed cases, of which those tagged `characterization` carry a `GREEN_ON_BASE` declaration, with 94 control cases alongside. `assume_gate_check.py`, `duplication_check.py`, `stranded_name_check.py --base origin/main` and the `mutation_check.py --refusals` census (baseline regenerated) pass.\n\n## Docs / CHANGELOG\n\nDocs updated: `styling-arbitrary-lengths.md` (type hints), `styling-flexbox-and-gap.md` (`grid-cols-[…]`), `styling-variants.md` (ring and outline bands), `styling-filters.md` (the blur row's bare number). CHANGELOG fragments `breaking/fix-caret-selection-alpha-modifier-3.md` (ring and outline defaults, `grid-cols-[5]`) and `unreleased/fix-caret-selection-alpha-modifier-3.md` (type hints). No single issue applies.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01FoK7YxdRjMGmfmRkEEmS88)_",
