          "distinct": true,
          "id": "5c043368361ebdbc20b90c6f4bb9dc0a367179f7",
          "message": "fix(velvet): mix a layoutId lead's border radii from the previous holder's and correct them for the scale it is drawn at (#1432)\n\n## What & why\n\nA `V.Motion` that takes a `layoutId` from another holder now mixes its four corner radii from that holder's to its own over the move, as Framer Motion's `mixValues` does:\n\n- A radius of none takes the other's unit, two radii of one unit mix and do not go below zero, and a pixel radius and a percent one do not mix, the lead's being taken.\n- A member drawn behind a crossfading lead takes the lead's radii.\n- A lead whose own move interrupts the mix holds the radii the mix had reached.\n\nA scaled Motion's pixel radius is divided by the scale it is drawn at, by the geometric mean of the two axes where they differ, since a style takes one length per corner where Framer writes a percent per axis. A percent radius is left as it is. Radii that would overlap on a side are scaled down together, as CSS scales radii, and `CornerRadiusFit` holds its fit while the projection writes the slots and refits what changed once they are handed back.\n\nA member following its lead does not read the lead's look on each pass, so that pass allocates nothing. `MotionTransitionSlots.Radius` is named by the layoutId projection alone, and a declared `Length` is read as covering it, so that no other play's held list loses the radius longhands. An inline `initial` radius is square before and during a move.\n\nA radius transition running as the projection starts writing is taken over from the engine. One still running as the move lands is stepped on past it. A `border-radius` shorthand in a transition list is read as the four longhands it covers, so the projection's own writes are not trailed by a transition of the shorthand.\n\nThis is the stacked successor of the rotate change that landed as #1428. Only the radius commit is new here. The branch is brought onto main by merge, with the engine-member reads rebased onto main's renamed declarations.\n\nRefs #1116\n\n## Tests\n\nThe new cases are in `MotionScheduledMechanicsTests`, bar one in `MotionNativeTransitionGuardSuspensionTests`. `base_red_check.py --plan --base origin/main` lists exactly the cases this branch wrote, 37 in all, and `Test ▸ base-red` shows the red ones. 12 of them are declared `[characterization]` (they hold on the base by design). They pin that a stylesheet-rounded or unrounded Motion, a percent radius, a spring overshoot and the like are left alone, and that a held per-property transition list keeps a corner radius when a driven Tween suspends every slot.\n\nLocal guards, all clean over the merged tree:\n\n- `assume_gate_check.py`\n- `duplication_check.py`, with its baseline regenerated, since three blocks moved between files\n- `stranded_name_check.py --base origin/main`\n- `mutation_check.py --refusals`, whose census differs from main only by the counts in `RunningStyleTransition.cs` and `StyleCascade.cs` that this change adds (baseline regenerated)\n- `tuple_assert_check.py`\n\nNo Unity editor was available, so neither suite was run locally. CI's `unity-tests` is the first run of this tree.\n\n## Docs and CHANGELOG\n\n- `Documentation~/motion.md` states the radius mix, the scale correction, the deviation from Framer's per-axis radius, and the run-on past the landing.\n- `Documentation~/player-builds.md` lists the new engine members.\n- The `Changelog~/unreleased` fragment `fix-1116-layoutid-tail-ported-4.md` is carried over.\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01FoK7YxdRjMGmfmRkEEmS88\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
