          "distinct": true,
          "id": "8149eb07ae06b614881500aa0d17ff4a0e3d68b6",
          "message": "fix(velvet)!: unmount the root on an error no boundary catches, and add MountOptions.OnUncaughtError (#1436)\n\n## What changed\n\nAn error that no error boundary catches now unmounts the whole tree `V.Mount` mounted, as React's root renders `null`. The tree's effect cleanups run as they do on any unmount, and the target is left empty. Before, the error was logged and the component that threw kept showing its last committed output.\n\n- **New `MountOptions.OnUncaughtError`** (React's `onUncaughtError`).\n  - It is called once the tree has unmounted, with the error and an `ErrorInfo` holding the component stack and an empty `ErrorBoundary`.\n  - Without a handler, the error is logged with `Debug.LogException`. In the Editor and in development builds, a warning naming the component that threw follows it. It names no component when the root itself threw.\n  - A cleanup that throws during that unmount is reported after the error that caused it.\n  - Errors thrown during `MountedTree.Dispose` are reported once every cleanup has run, as React reports what `root.unmount()` raises after its commit.\n- **A cleanup error in a removed subtree goes past the boundaries that the removal deletes.** It goes to the nearest ancestor outside the deletion, where React's commit-phase capture starts. Before, a boundary inside the removed subtree caught it, and the report was then dropped with that boundary.\n- **A boundary owns the errors of its fallback swap.** An error thrown while a boundary swaps its fallback in, or disposes the failed output, is now that boundary's own. It is reported after the caught error, and the fallback renders again with it.\n- **When a boundary's fallback content throws** and nothing above catches it, the root takes it, and only the content's error is reported. React discards that catch the same way.\n- **Errors under a torn-down ancestor are no longer dropped.** The boundary search now passes over fibers that are already torn down.\n- **Breaking: a component stack ends at the outermost component**, leaving out the root `V.Mount` makes, as React's stack leaves out the HostRoot. An error the root raises itself has an empty stack.\n- **Breaking: `MountOptions` options are `init` properties.** `new MountOptions(handler)` becomes `new MountOptions { OnCaughtError = handler }`.\n- **Velvet deviation:** React calls `onUncaughtError` before the unmounted components' `useEffect` cleanups. Velvet runs those cleanups as each component unmounts, so they have already run when the handler is called.\n\n## Tests\n\n- `UncaughtErrorRootTests` and `UncaughtErrorHandlerTests` are new.\n- `BoundaryCatchScopeTests` covers swap ownership and a removed boundary's cleanup error reaching the boundary above.\n- Error-boundary, Suspense and transition cases are updated for the root's catch.\n- Cases whose only change is the `MountOptions` spelling are declared `GREEN_ON_BASE(refactor)`.\n\n## Documentation\n\n- `react-migration.md`: the `onCaughtError` and `onUncaughtError` rows.\n- The README index.\n- CHANGELOG fragments under `Changelog~/breaking` and `Changelog~/unreleased`.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01FoK7YxdRjMGmfmRkEEmS88)_",
