          "distinct": true,
          "id": "8e783b00a6da7a4d7091567597799c04c9e839bb",
          "message": "fix(velvet): carry a layoutId Motion's own translate and scale on the transitions it declares (#1434)\n\n## What changed\n\nA `V.Motion` moving under a `layoutId` composes the move's translate and scale with its own. Its own values used to be read once, from `resolvedStyle`, when the projection was created, and never refreshed. That caused four problems:\n\n- A class change of `translate-*` or `scale-*` during the move stayed hidden until the move landed.\n- A lead handed over in render read the transform it had before that render.\n- A translate or scale transition that was already running froze or jumped when the move started.\n- A follower that took the lead back started from the transform it had been drawn at over the old leader.\n\nThe element's own translate and scale are now carried the way rotate and border radius already are:\n\n- **Start:** the carry starts from the value drawn when the slot is first written. A follower that takes the lead back starts from the translate, scale and rotate it hands back, rather than from the style it was drawn at.\n- **Running transitions:** a translate or scale transition that UI Toolkit is already running is taken over, including one running in percent.\n- **Timing:** a change during the move runs on the element's declared transition, or on a variant swap's held list. Translate and scale each retarget as one value, as UI Toolkit runs them.\n- **Landing:** a change still running when the move lands runs on to its end, as rotate and radii already do.\n- **Percent translate:** a percent translate is carried in percent, so it follows the element's size on every frame.\n\n`StyleCascade` gains readers for the cascaded translate and scale, beside its rotate reader. Outside IL2CPP they read through compiled accessors and allocate nothing.\n\nThe box-shadow correction tracked under #1116 is not part of this change. A `V.Motion` never paints a shadow (`shadow-*` on a Motion is warned and ignored), and Framer Motion corrects only a projected element's own shadow, so Velvet already matches it there.\n\n## Tests\n\n- `MotionScheduledMechanicsTests` covers:\n  - the takeover of running transitions, in pixels and in percent;\n  - a change during the move running on its declared timing, retargeted as one value, including a single-axis reverse;\n  - leads handed back during a render;\n  - followers that take the lead back, for translate, scale and rotate;\n  - run-on past the landing;\n  - a percent translate following its box;\n  - a zero-size box;\n  - records that do not outlive their render.\n- `LayoutIdLookAcrossParentsTests` pins the look that a holder joining under another parent mixes from.\n- `StyleCascadeTransformReadTests` pins that the compiled readers allocate nothing.\n\n## Documentation\n\n- `motion.md` and `player-builds.md` are updated.\n- CHANGELOG fragment: `Changelog~/unreleased/fix-1116-own-transform-and-shadow-5.md`.\n\nRefs #1116\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01FoK7YxdRjMGmfmRkEEmS88\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
