          "distinct": true,
          "id": "2521188064c37606fa98eddad7e61db8d3a4e606",
          "message": "fix(velvet)!: paint a dashed divider at the child's own width, color and style, in Chrome's dash pattern (#1438)\n\n## What changed\n\nA `divide-dashed` or `divide-dotted` divider now draws at the border width and colour that win the divided edge. The width is the child's own width class or bracket width. The colour is the child's own colour from classes, theme or hover rules, inline code, or a `V.Motion` drive.\n\n- The divider takes the child's own `border-solid`, `border-dashed` or `border-dotted` over the divide's style, unless the divide's style is important.\n- A colour the child's code writes inline outranks a plain divide colour on a solid or a dashed edge, and outranks the child's colour classes on a dashed edge. It survives the divider switching between dashed and solid.\n- An important declaration and a motion drive keep their precedence.\n\nDashes and dots for dividers, `border-dashed` and `border-dotted` now follow the pattern Chrome uses for a border side:\n- the dash-to-gap ratio depends on the width;\n- the gap is fitted so that a line starts and ends on a dash;\n- a line too short for the pattern falls back to solid;\n- dots up to 3px are square, with Chrome's whole-pixel end-dot adjustments.\n\nEach side of a dashed or dotted border, and a dashed divider on a rounded child, is painted along its own line or along the rounded outline and cut at its corner miter, so a translucent colour is laid down only once where two sides meet.\n\n## Tests\n\n- `DashedBorderPainterTests` and `DashedBorderSideTests` cover the dash and dot geometry and the corner cut.\n- `DivideClassParityTests` covers the child's width, colour and style precedence, the code-written colour, the rounded divided side, and the capture under a mask.\n\n## Documentation\n\n- `styling-flexbox-and-gap.md` and `player-builds.md` are updated.\n- Changelog: `Changelog~/breaking/fix-1118-dashed-divider-ported-2.md`, plus a correction to `fix-1118-flex-parity.md`.\n\nRefs #1118\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01FoK7YxdRjMGmfmRkEEmS88)_",
