          "distinct": true,
          "id": "7455fc9f4d96a5299d6c298a3fe39b7970103e93",
          "message": "fix(velvet)!: read an important modifier after the variants, as Tailwind does (#1439)\n\n## What changed\n\nVelvet now reads an important modifier where Tailwind v4 reads it: on the utility, after every variant.\n\n- `hover:!p-[52px] hover:!pt-2` puts 8px of top padding while hovered, not 52px.\n- `selection:!bg-red-500` colours the text selection.\n- `hover:!border-8` reserves its inset on the particle and skew layers.\n- A `!` in front of the variants (`!hover:w-4`, `!selection:bg-red-500`) leaves the class inert, because Tailwind generates no rule for it. **Breaking:** `!selection:bg-*` used to colour the selection.\n- A token with an empty variant (`:!w-4`, `hover::!w-4`) is left whole.\n- The spacing rewrite spells an important variant token as Tailwind does (`sm:!pt-[8px]`).\n\nThe branch also adds specs for a motion pose layered over an element's own rejected composed family, for example an exit pose `translate-y-4` over an own `translate-y-[10]`.\n\nThis carries over the part of `fix/caret-selection-alpha-modifier-5` that still applies on main. The rest of that branch rewrote rejected composed families during normalization, which the runtime rejection layers on main replace.\n\n## Docs\n\n- `styling-variants.md`: a `!` ahead of the variants leaves the class inert.\n- `Changelog~/unreleased` and `Changelog~/breaking` fragments added.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01FoK7YxdRjMGmfmRkEEmS88)_",
