          "distinct": true,
          "id": "c7b996f0abbb3d298032def7f09c5f1129dedf25",
          "message": "feat(velvet)!: resolve CSS custom properties written as classes and in arbitrary values (#1444)\n\nRefs #1378\n\n## What changed\n\n- `var()` in arbitrary values and Tailwind v4's `(--x)` shorthand now resolve as the browser resolves them:\n  - in sizes, colours, modifiers, shorthands and painted utilities;\n  - in a fallback that contains a function, such as `w-(--w,calc(6px*2))`.\n- A custom property written as a class sets the variable, and its readers follow when it changes.\n- When a `var()` cannot be resolved, the property it is in falls back to unset, as CSS does.\n- A type hint in a modifier's shorthand is declined, as Tailwind declines it.\n\n## Docs\n\n`styling-custom-properties.md`, `styling-arbitrary-lengths.md`, `fonts.md`, and fragments in `Changelog~/unreleased` and `Changelog~/breaking`.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01FoK7YxdRjMGmfmRkEEmS88)_",
