          "distinct": true,
          "id": "7cb0b91a093eff8040b9e5eac3033a6ee09c222e",
          "message": "feat(velvet): warn on a keyless child built into a list, as React does (VEL600) (#1446)\n\nCloses #1113\n\n## What changed\n\nReact warns when an element in an array has no key. This adds the equivalent warning, the new analyzer VEL600 (category `Velvet.Reconciler`). It reports a `V.*` node built without a key when the node reaches a children array through any of these:\n- a `Select`;\n- a local variable;\n- a helper method;\n- a delegate;\n- a `List<VNode>` that is turned into an array.\n\nLike React, it does not report text nodes (`V.Text`) or children written out directly. `V.When` is checked through to the node its factory builds.\n\nThe package's own tests no longer produce any VEL600 warnings. Three Motion lists now have keys. Eight members whose tests depend on rows being matched by position have the warning suppressed in one file.\n\n## Docs\n\nThe reconciler guide and the diagnostic table are updated, and the changelog fragment is extended.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01FoK7YxdRjMGmfmRkEEmS88)_",
