          "distinct": true,
          "id": "12d23f41ec33ca27b71895f418855ef9e206bea1",
          "message": "fix(velvet)!: step focus groups in hierarchy order, append portal panels to the Tab order, and render FocusScope without a wrapper (#1451)\n\n## What changed\n- Arrow keys inside a `singleTabStop` group step through members in hierarchy order, with an opt-in `wrap:` (FO7, FO15).\n- A chained-portal Tab escape blurs the source and focuses the target in the same dispatch (FO4).\n- `V.Portal(layer:)` and `V.WorldSpace` default to `PanelFocusOrder.Appended`, so host content follows the tree in Tab order as a `document.body` portal does; `V.DragOverlay` stays `Isolated` (P9).\n- `V.FocusScope` renders no wrapper element; the scope is bounded by two hidden markers around its children (FO14). Its element arguments are removed.\n- A panel forgets an element moved to another panel (F-pool-3); an element released while gaining focus is scrubbed on the next tick (F-pool-5).\n- FO5, FO9, FO11, FO13, F-bounce, F-pool-2 and F-pool-4 were already resolved on main.\n\nBreaking changes are recorded in `Changelog~/breaking/fix-1123-focus-parity.md`.\n\n## Docs\n`focus.md`, `portals.md`, `react-migration.md`, `drag-and-drop.md`, `Documentation~/README.md`.\n\nCloses #1123\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01FoK7YxdRjMGmfmRkEEmS88)_",
