          "distinct": true,
          "id": "e9633ee4dc6afc34efe3fdec66c0e9b5639d0d53",
          "message": "fix(velvet)!: bring flexbox, gap and divide in line with Tailwind v4 and CSS (#1452)\n\n## What changed\n- A gap on an element with no direction class spaces the column the engine lays it out in (F1).\n- A wrapping gap container with a definite size grows its declared width, height, min and max by the gap, so items wrap and sit where CSS puts them.\n- F7, F8, F9, F10, F13, F14 and F15 are resolved; F2, F4, F6, F11, F12 and F17 were already resolved on main.\n- F3 (no gap in the layout engine's style data) and F16 (`display` takes only flex and none) stay documented: `FlexEngineLayoutStyleTests` pins both engine facts.\n\nBreaking changes are recorded in new `Changelog~/breaking/fix-1118-flex-parity-*.md` fragments.\n\n## Docs\nThe flexbox/gap guide and its `Documentation~/README.md` row.\n\nCloses #1118\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01FoK7YxdRjMGmfmRkEEmS88)_",
