          "distinct": true,
          "id": "bdcf8e017eb66ebe9055de5cbcb41d6736cbcbe0",
          "message": "fix(velvet)!: portal and anchored parity with drei and React portals (#1459)\n\nCloses #1122\n\n## What changed\n- `distanceFactor` scales by the camera's view size: 2·tan(fov/2)·distance for a perspective camera and 2·orthographicSize for an orthographic one.\n- `V.Anchored` places itself through its parent's world-to-local transform, so it works under a scaled or rotated parent.\n- Velvet no longer adds its own collider to a world-space panel, because `UIDocument` already keeps one.\n- A destroyed layer or world-space host is rebuilt on the next patch of a portal that targets it, and the portal's children remount into it.\n- The warning for an unregistered layer id now says when the children will mount.\n\nBreaking changes: `Changelog~/breaking/fix-1122.md` and `Changelog~/breaking/fix-1122-anchored-wrapper.md`. Docs updated alongside.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01FoK7YxdRjMGmfmRkEEmS88)_",
