          "distinct": true,
          "id": "82ec0d6e1f4b70aa9c98b210003a023114f206d7",
          "message": "fix(velvet): pick skewed elements by their sheared shape, fit every radius, rank user classes (#1461)\n\nRefs #1117\n\n## What changed\n- A skewed `V.Div`, `V.Button` or label is now picked by its sheared quadrilateral rather than by its bounding rectangle. These three are built as pick-shaped subclasses whose shape `FiberSkewApplier` sets and pool reset clears.\n- The corner-radius fit now covers every element, including a radius written by a stylesheet or in code, not only `rounded-*` classes.\n- A user-written class that the bundled table does not name is probed for the longhands it writes, so it competes per longhand with Velvet's payloads.\n- A play class that the seed adopted as a base entry is no longer left behind when a payload of the same class turns off.\n\n## Breaking\nRecorded in `Changelog~/breaking/fix-1117-rest.md`. Div, Button and Label elements are now subclasses. The radius fit attaches to every element. User classes rank per longhand.\n\n## Docs\n`styling-variants.md` and the README row are updated.\n\n## Still open on #1117\nComposing the shear with `rotate-*`, `scale-*`, `animate-*` and `V.Motion` is not done; those cases keep the painted layer.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01FoK7YxdRjMGmfmRkEEmS88)_",
