          "message": "fix(velvet)!: Framer Motion parity for motion presets and lengths (#1454)\n\nCloses #1115\n\n## What & why\n- Font-size (`text-*`) and letter-spacing (`tracking-*`) presets are animated channels, pinned against the bundled stylesheets.\n- `rounded-full` animates to the stylesheet radius; `-full` sizing/position/basis classes animate as 100%.\n- Spring and Bezier plays animate shadow, skew and gradient paint layers (z swaps at the end), keyframe presets and `useAnimate` are added.\n- Percent and fraction translates (`translate-x-1/2`, `translate-x-full`, `translate-x-[50%]`) animate in percent, keeping each axis's unit through handover and interruption.\n\nBreaking changes: `Changelog~/breaking/claude-issue-1115-motion-presets.md`. `Documentation~/motion.md` updated.\n\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [ ] Tests pass locally (EditMode / PlayMode / generator tests as applicable) — not run locally (no Unity editor available); the EditMode/PlayMode suites run in CI on this head\n- [ ] New regression tests were verified red without the change and green with it — measured by `Test ▸ base-red` on the merge base, pending on this head\n- [x] Docs are updated for every fact this change touches (guides, READMEs, CLAUDE.md) — or this PR has no doc impact\n- [x] CHANGELOG fragment added for behavior/perf changes, named for the branch with `/` as `-` — inline under `## [Unreleased]` on a maintenance line with no `scripts/release/compile_changelog.py` (pure refactors are omitted by convention)\n- [x] Known gaps or deliberate deferrals discovered here are filed as issues with acceptance criteria — none deferred\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01FoK7YxdRjMGmfmRkEEmS88\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
