          "distinct": true,
          "id": "64d585a1331d09a34ce383b6e6d612799e949b6e",
          "message": "fix(velvet): compose skew-* with rotate, scale, animate-* and V.Motion on the element's own transform (#1462)\n\n## What & why\n\nA `skew-*` element that also carried a `rotate-*` or `scale-*` class (behind a variant too), an `animate-*` preset or a `V.Motion` fell back to a painted silhouette layer. In that layer:\n\n- the caster's text neither sheared nor moved;\n- descendants were seated with an inline `translate` instead of being sheared;\n- `origin-*` did not move the pivot;\n- the hit region did not lean.\n\nCSS applies the individual `rotate` and `scale` properties and then `transform: skewX() skewY()`, so the element's linear part is R(θ)·diag(sx, sy)·K.\n\n- `SkewTransformFactor.TryFactor` now factors any 2x2 matrix into the inline `rotate` (one 3D rotation) and `scale` slots. A negative determinant is carried in the scale's y.\n- A new per-element `AuthoredTransform` keeps the rotate/scale each writer intends apart from what the slots hold. Every writer goes through it:\n  - the arbitrary-value resolver;\n  - the `animate-*` loops;\n  - the Spring/Bezier drivers;\n  - the gesture mask;\n  - the anchored and sortable-drag writers;\n  - the `layoutId` and `V.Motion` paths.\n\n  Readers that took the inline slot as the authored value read it back through the same record. Without a skew the writes are unchanged.\n- The rotate/scale a `rotate-*`/`scale-*` class declares is read off the class list and recomposed on every class diff and variant toggle. Skew angles a `V.Motion` animates are written into the same slots.\n- Nothing reaches the painted skew layer any more, so it is removed: the silhouette binding, the child-seating translate manipulator, the gradient silhouette baker and its shader. The shadow, border and gradient appliers no longer defer to a skew binding. This is breaking for anyone relying on the painted layer's output, so a `Changelog~/breaking` fragment is included.\n\nDocs: `styling-variants.md` (skew section and deviation table), `motion.md`, `styling-shadows.md`, `styling-gradients.md`, `player-builds.md` (shader count), and the `Documentation~/README.md` index.\n\nRefs #1117\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [ ] Tests pass locally (EditMode / PlayMode / generator tests as applicable). Not run locally (no Unity editor available); CI `Test ▸ unity-tests` is the verification.\n- [ ] New regression tests were verified red without the change and green with it. Measured by `Test ▸ base-red` on this PR.\n- [x] Docs are updated for every fact this change touches (guides, READMEs, CLAUDE.md) — or this PR has no doc impact\n- [x] CHANGELOG fragment added for behavior/perf changes, named for the branch with `/` as `-` — inline under `## [Unreleased]` on a maintenance line with no `scripts/release/compile_changelog.py` (pure refactors are omitted by convention)\n- [ ] Known gaps or deliberate deferrals discovered here are filed as issues with acceptance criteria\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01FoK7YxdRjMGmfmRkEEmS88)_",
