          "distinct": true,
          "id": "9b6e13fe1f6de6ad0c946654fe2ae6817f9f957e",
          "message": "feat(velvet): weave independent reactive scopes per component (#1464)\n\n## What & why\n\nThe compiler weaver used to put a single all-or-nothing gate on each component. A single changed dependency rebuilt the whole VNode tree, so the reconciler's reference-identity bail never fired inside the body.\n\nThis change splits a component body into independent reactive scopes:\n\n- **Runtime:** a multi-slot per-fiber cache, `MemoScopeCache`, behind `Hooks.ReserveScopes` / `TryGetScope` / `StoreScope`, reset when a fiber returns to the pool. `TryGetMemoizedVNode` / `StoreMemoizedVNode` stay as the one-scope form.\n- **Weaver:** infers scopes from the IL. Each VNode-building call that reads only outside values and writes nothing outside itself gets its own cache slot, keyed on exactly what it reads. Scopes can nest. A hook-returned tuple is keyed per element, a props record per member, and a lambda closure per field.\n- **Bail rules:** a dispatch ahead of the gate, an unresolvable callee, and a positional hook outside the allow-lists now cost only the outer gate, so independent scopes stay cached. Conditional hooks, loops, hooks inside try/catch/finally, and a return before a hook still refuse.\n- **Reporting:** each `[Component]` method carries `MemoizationReportAttribute` with its bailout reasons. `AssemblyMetadata(\"Velvet.MemoizationReport\", \"warn\")` also raises them as build warnings.\n\nDocs: `Documentation~/memoization.md`, `Documentation~/react-migration.md`, the README index and `AGENTS.md`. The changelog fragment is `Changelog~/unreleased/feat-421-reactive-scopes.md`; rendered output is unchanged.\n\nCloses #421\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Tests pass locally (EditMode / PlayMode / generator tests as applicable) — generator tests are green locally; the Unity suites run in CI\n- [x] New regression tests were verified red without the change and green with it — the new fixtures call APIs absent on the base\n- [x] Docs are updated for every fact this change touches (guides, READMEs, CLAUDE.md) — or this PR has no doc impact\n- [x] CHANGELOG fragment added for behavior/perf changes, named for the branch with `/` as `-` — inline under `## [Unreleased]` on a maintenance line with no `scripts/release/compile_changelog.py` (pure refactors are omitted by convention)\n- [x] Known gaps or deliberate deferrals discovered here are filed as issues with acceptance criteria\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01FoK7YxdRjMGmfmRkEEmS88)_",
