          "distinct": true,
          "id": "864a463efec3cebd9ecd92bc8b450cc15be1bc1d",
          "message": "feat(velvet)!: accept cubic-bezier x control points outside [0,1] (#1472)\n\n## What & why\n\nA Motion `cubicBezier` whose x1 or x2 lay outside [0,1] was rejected: it fell back to the default curve and logged a warning. Motion accepts any control point.\n\n- `CubicBezierEvaluator.Evaluate` accepts any finite x1/x2. Outside [0,1] it finds the curve parameter by bisection, because Newton steps can leave the interval on such a curve. A non-finite coordinate still falls back to the default curve with the warning.\n- The CSS `cubic-bezier()` token in `animate-` classes still requires x in [0,1], as CSS does.\n- Docs: `Documentation~/motion.md`. Changelog: `Changelog~/breaking/feat-1327-motion-parity.md`.\n\nThis is the breaking item of #1327. Its additive items remain open there.\n\nRefs #1327\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Tests pass locally (EditMode / PlayMode / generator tests as applicable) — the Unity suites run in CI\n- [x] New regression tests were verified red without the change and green with it — via the base-red lane\n- [x] Docs are updated for every fact this change touches (guides, READMEs, CLAUDE.md) — or this PR has no doc impact\n- [x] CHANGELOG fragment added for behavior/perf changes, named for the branch with `/` as `-` — inline under `## [Unreleased]` on a maintenance line with no `scripts/release/compile_changelog.py` (pure refactors are omitted by convention)\n- [x] Known gaps or deliberate deferrals discovered here are filed as issues with acceptance criteria\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01FoK7YxdRjMGmfmRkEEmS88)_",
