          "distinct": true,
          "id": "7ecd9360a7c0e1715f99ebfb1d639c2568762c29",
          "message": "fix(velvet)!: keep a text flex item's content floor under an explicit min-size auto (#1471)\n\n## What & why\n\nAn explicit `min-w-[auto]` or `min-h-[auto]` on a text flex item stood down the automatic minimum that keeps its content from shrinking. Under CSS, `auto` is that minimum.\n\n- `StyleFlexMinSizeManipulator`:\n  - `min-w-[auto]`, `min-h-[auto]` and the new `min-w-auto` / `min-h-auto` declare no minimum, so they keep the floor.\n  - Which class wins follows the cascade order of the utilities (`StyleRuleOrder`), not the order they are written in.\n  - A slot another writer overwrote is no longer held.\n- `_sizing.uss` gains `.min-w-auto` and `.min-h-auto`. `StyleUtilityProperties.g.cs` and the stylesheet census are regenerated.\n- A variant such as `md:` or `hover:` that toggles a sizing, `overflow-` or `truncate` class now rescans the floor.\n- Docs: `Documentation~/styling-flexbox-and-gap.md`. Changelog: `Changelog~/breaking/fix-1348-min-size-auto-floor.md`. Code that relied on `min-w-[auto]` to let a label shrink now needs `min-w-0`.\n\nCloses #1348\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Tests pass locally (EditMode / PlayMode / generator tests as applicable) — generator tests locally; Unity suites in CI\n- [x] New regression tests were verified red without the change and green with it — via the base-red lane\n- [x] Docs are updated for every fact this change touches (guides, READMEs, CLAUDE.md) — or this PR has no doc impact\n- [x] CHANGELOG fragment added for behavior/perf changes, named for the branch with `/` as `-` — inline under `## [Unreleased]` on a maintenance line with no `scripts/release/compile_changelog.py` (pure refactors are omitted by convention)\n- [x] Known gaps or deliberate deferrals discovered here are filed as issues with acceptance criteria\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01FoK7YxdRjMGmfmRkEEmS88)_",
