          "distinct": true,
          "id": "3d966b37981e109925ad219895d184828a3e932f",
          "message": "feat(velvet)!: commit a root 404, make route ids unique, and add the match hooks (#1474)\n\n## What & why\n\nThree router behaviours diverged from the data router's:\n\n- **Unmatched path:** it returned `NotFound` without committing anything. It now commits the location and a history entry, with the root route carrying an `ErrorResponse` 404 that its `errorElement` (or the default) renders. Guards, actions and loaders do not run, and loader data is cleared. A guard redirect to an unmatched path commits the same way.\n- **Route ids:** `RouteId` values collided. An id is now `RouteDefinition.Id`, else the tree position (`\"0\"`, `\"0-1\"`). A duplicate id throws. Loader data, action data and errors re-key accordingly.\n- **Pathless layouts:** a pathless layout with children no longer matches as a leaf of its own.\n\nAdditive:\n- `RouteDefinition.Id` and `Handle`, also on `V.Route`.\n- The hooks `Hooks.UseMatches`, `UseRouteLoaderData<T>`, `UseResolvedPath`, `UseHref`, `UseNavigationType` and `UseInRouterContext`.\n\nDocs: `Documentation~/routing.md` and the README index. Changelog: `Changelog~/breaking/feat-1326-router-parity.md` and `Changelog~/unreleased/feat-1326-router-parity.md`. Existing tests that pinned the uncommitted 404 or the old ids are updated.\n\nThe remaining additive items of #1326 stay open there.\n\nRefs #1326\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Tests pass locally (EditMode / PlayMode / generator tests as applicable) — generator tests locally; Unity suites in CI\n- [x] New regression tests were verified red without the change and green with it — via the base-red lane\n- [x] Docs are updated for every fact this change touches (guides, READMEs, CLAUDE.md) — or this PR has no doc impact\n- [x] CHANGELOG fragment added for behavior/perf changes, named for the branch with `/` as `-` — inline under `## [Unreleased]` on a maintenance line with no `scripts/release/compile_changelog.py` (pure refactors are omitted by convention)\n- [x] Known gaps or deliberate deferrals discovered here are filed as issues with acceptance criteria\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01FoK7YxdRjMGmfmRkEEmS88)_",
