          "distinct": true,
          "id": "8a5dcfbab462ef0f7a1849441fb4e5fe9ec1b04b",
          "message": "fix(velvet)!: keep a revealed Suspense's content when a transition suspends it (#1470)\n\n## What & why\n\nA transition-lane render that suspended a boundary already showing its content swapped that content for the fallback. It now keeps the revealed content, leaves the transition pending, and commits the new content once the resource settles.\n\n- `ExpandSuspenseInline` gives up the pass for a transition-lane suspend of a revealed primary, and rolls the primary expansion back. The extracted `RetainsPrimary` decides that case.\n- `SuspendPassOwner` gives up a transition pass under a revealed outer boundary instead of asking that boundary to render, so the retry on resolve renders the update. This also holds for a transition started below the boundary.\n- `FiberRenderer.BeginPass` clears the decline flag at the start of every pass.\n- Unchanged: an urgent or normal update still shows the fallback, and so do a boundary that has not revealed yet and a newly mounted nested boundary. A rejection reaches the error boundary.\n- Docs: `Documentation~/react-migration.md`. Changelog: `Changelog~/breaking/fix-407-transition-keeps-revealed.md`.\n- `TimeSlicedFiberTests` pinned the old request-the-boundary behaviour. That case is renamed and flipped.\n\nCloses #407\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Tests pass locally (EditMode / PlayMode / generator tests as applicable) — the Unity suites run in CI\n- [x] New regression tests were verified red without the change and green with it — via the base-red lane\n- [x] Docs are updated for every fact this change touches (guides, READMEs, CLAUDE.md) — or this PR has no doc impact\n- [x] CHANGELOG fragment added for behavior/perf changes, named for the branch with `/` as `-` — inline under `## [Unreleased]` on a maintenance line with no `scripts/release/compile_changelog.py` (pure refactors are omitted by convention)\n- [x] Known gaps or deliberate deferrals discovered here are filed as issues with acceptance criteria\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01FoK7YxdRjMGmfmRkEEmS88)_",
