          "id": "30e742954e391d5c2c7422c983d71b8b4cdb3e5d",
          "message": "test(velvet): answer the remaining mutation survivors in the effect view and inspect overlay (#1482)\n\n## What & why\n\n- `PreviewInspectOverlayTests`: six cases pin `UpdateLabel` — label displayed after a refresh, top edge above the margin box (exact offset), below it when above would clip, exactly at the top edge, hidden when nothing is measured, and left empty when the bridge has no root. They target the `display = Flex` removal, the two `-` arithmetic mutants, the `<` to `<=` boundary, the hide-line removal and the `==` flips in the guard.\n- `ParticlesPlaybackTests` (PlayMode): reads `aliveParticleCount` of the clone after `Stop` instead of pixels. The existing Play/Stop case is ignored on a device that cannot draw a graph, which is why the `Reinit` call in `ParticlesEffectView.Stop` survived; the particle count needs only the simulation.\n- Not answered by a test: the three non-terminating mutants (the `Add` removal in `SetTargetExtent`, `fiber = fiber.Parent` in `DragOverlayHost`, `current = ...` in `ComponentBoundarySearch`). Each spins forever on the main thread in cases that already exist, so a new test cannot make them fail faster. The verdict is \"hung\" only when `baseline * 3 <= --timeout`; the particle shard's baseline of 368 s against 900 s makes it \"timed out\" instead. That needs a larger `--timeout` for those shards, not a test.\n\nAll new cases are declared `GREEN_ON_BASE(characterization)`; their RED evidence is the mutation campaign. Not run locally: no Unity editor in this environment.\n\nNo doc or CHANGELOG impact (test-only).\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Tests pass locally (EditMode / PlayMode / generator tests as applicable) — Unity suites run in CI\n- [x] New regression tests were verified red without the change and green with it — kills are decided by the next mutation record run\n- [x] Docs are updated for every fact this change touches (guides, READMEs, CLAUDE.md) — or this PR has no doc impact\n- [x] CHANGELOG fragment added for behavior/perf changes — none needed, test-only\n- [x] Known gaps or deliberate deferrals discovered here are filed as issues with acceptance criteria\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01FoK7YxdRjMGmfmRkEEmS88)_",
