          "id": "6e93b43347ff9ed900b29fc0bbadb7bac05ff5fc",
          "message": "test(velvet): pin the CodeGen weaver behaviours its mutants showed unchecked (#1487)\n\n## What & why\n\nA mutation run over `CodeGen/` left 22 of its 24 mutants alive: no case of the EditMode suite noticed them (the other two were killed by a timeout, `Solve` never terminating).\n\n`ReactiveScopeSelectionTests` reads the `MemoizationReportAttribute` the weaver leaves on a component, or the woven IL of one, and renders once. It kills 17 of the 22:\n\n- a custom hook composing only value hooks, and a framework static outside the pure list (`HookKindOf`, `OfPlainCall`);\n- a hook value aliased by a ref local, and a getter called on a struct state's address (`PropagateAddress`, `ReadsOnly`);\n- a store into an array the run did not make, a local read after the scope that assigned it, and a struct built in place (`Produce`, `IndexAccesses`, `InitializesLocal`, `Normalize`, `ReadLocal`, `ScopeDependency.Key`);\n- a try or a throwing switch ahead of the tail, a scope inside a try, and a conditional expression that opens the body (`ReactiveScopeFlow.Continue`, `CheckHandlers`, `ExtendOverEntries`);\n- a field read off a state object, which is the one case that renders (`ReadLocal`).\n\nThe other five are answered where they sit with `MUTANT_SURVIVES`:\n\n- `equivalent`: the void-hook guard in `DirectHookKind` (no reader of `CallKind` tells `EffectHook` from `ReactiveHook`) and the pass bound in `ExtendOverEntries`.\n- `unreachable`: `Walk`'s unreached-instruction branch, the self-branch loop head in `LoopHeads`, and the end-of-body test in `CheckHost`. Each changes behaviour only for an instruction nothing reaches, or a body that falls off its end. `Given_EveryComponentBodyThisAssemblyHolds_When_TheFlowWalkReadsIt_Then_NoInstructionIsUnreachedAndNoneFallsOffTheEnd` pins that no component body of the test assembly holds either, and the declarations name it.\n\nEvery new case carries `GREEN_ON_BASE(characterization)`: each pins behaviour the base already has, and its comment names the cut that reddens it.\n\nDocs: no impact. This adds tests and comments only, with no behaviour or guide change.\nCHANGELOG: no fragment. Nothing user-visible changes.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [ ] Tests pass locally (EditMode / PlayMode / generator tests as applicable). No Unity editor was available to the author, so CI's `Test ▸ unity-tests` is the first run of the new fixture inside the editor. The 13 report and IL cases were run beforehand against the real weaver sources outside Unity, on the base and on each of the 22 mutants, compiled with and without optimization.\n- [x] New regression tests were verified red without the change and green with it. They characterize existing behaviour, so they are green on the base by design; the mutants stand in for the red run.\n- [x] Docs are updated for every fact this change touches (guides, READMEs, CLAUDE.md) — or this PR has no doc impact\n- [x] CHANGELOG fragment added for behavior/perf changes, named for the branch with `/` as `-` — none needed: test and comment changes only\n- [x] Known gaps or deliberate deferrals discovered here are filed as issues with acceptance criteria. None filed from this change.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01FoK7YxdRjMGmfmRkEEmS88)_",
