          "distinct": true,
          "id": "fc7fa8803da510f487b20842cd8656896c2a2065",
          "message": "perf(velvet): drop the reconciler's per-element table scans and chain walks (#1494)\n\nBuilds on #1493 (which contains #1491); the diff against `main` includes theirs until they merge.\n\n## What & why\n\n- `ComponentFiber` keeps the link before each child, so `RemoveChild` is O(1) instead of a walk from the first child. Append, `CommitChildOrder` and removal maintain it; `AppendChild` of a child the parent already holds now unlinks it first (the old path cut the chain at the child).\n- Suspense and AnimatePresence records are pruned through an index of the elements they name (a superset: a retired record leaves its entry until a prune drops it). Tearing down an element no record names reads no table and rents no list. `PresenceStates` entries now join through `RegisterPresenceState` / `SetPresenceOwningPortal`.\n- `ReorderToNewElementOrder` returns before building a position table of the container (and before three more scans) when every element is an anchor, i.e. a keyed re-render that moves nothing.\n- `LogicalChildSlots.IsInvisible` asks the z-layer table once rather than twice per child.\n\nNot changed: the create path (1,000 rows, ~221k GC.Alloc blocks). No profiler was available, and the per-element registrations I read (`CornerRadiusFit.Observe`, text-input tracking) carry behaviour, so no cut could be shown safe.\n\n## Tests\n\n`ChildElementPlacementReorderTests` (hash counts of the children, 0 on an all-anchor pass), `ComponentFiberPreviousLinkTests`, `ContainerKeyedStatePruneIndexTests`. Nothing was run locally (no Unity editor here); CI is the first compile and the first run. The cases that call `RegisterPresenceState` / `SetPresenceOwningPortal` cannot build on the merge base, so their red is not shown by `base-red`.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [ ] Tests pass locally (EditMode / PlayMode / generator tests as applicable) - not run locally, no editor available\n- [ ] New regression tests were verified red without the change and green with it - left to CI\n- [x] Docs are updated for every fact this change touches - no doc impact\n- [x] CHANGELOG fragment added (`claude-perf-reconciler-slow-paths.md`)\n- [x] Known gaps or deliberate deferrals discovered here are filed as issues with acceptance criteria - none filed; create-path allocations and the O(1) invisible marker are deferred\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01FoK7YxdRjMGmfmRkEEmS88)_",
