          "distinct": true,
          "id": "f19daf256b62e5a4e5c41e66e84434f88cb33280",
          "message": "perf(velvet): leave the callbacks of a discarded row's descendants registered (#1498)\n\n## What & why\n\nClearing a list of 1,000 rows (`Clear_1000Rows` of the js-framework-benchmark port) took about two and a half times as long as creating them. A per-stage profile of the editor PlayMode run, taken with temporary instrumentation that is not part of this change, put 84 to 90% of the clear in two places: removing the text-leaf manipulators (`StyleFlexMinSizeManipulator`, 3,000 removals, 0.33 ms each on the slower of two runners) and unwiring the Button click gate (2,000 Buttons, six `UnregisterCallback` calls each, 0.13 ms per Button on the faster). The earlier hypothesis, a quadratic registry or slot walk, was not the cause: the tree-return and registry stages were about 2 ms of 1,100.\n\nBoth are `UnregisterCallback` on an element that leaves with its row. In a probe in the same editor run, one unregistration cost about 6, 10 and 36 microseconds with 250, 1,000 and 4,000 elements alive, so the time one takes grows with how many were made before it. The record each unregistration hands back to Unity is what `UnregisterCallbackRecordPoolTests` pins.\n\n`FiberElementCleaner.RemoveElement` now names the removed element the root of a discarded teardown when nothing pools it afterwards and no Portal range inside it is torn out through `CleanupPortal`. Below that root, the Button click gate and `StyleTextItemManipulator` leave their callbacks registered. A removal whose root is pooled (a Button or Label row), a nested teardown, and a subtree holding a Portal target unregister as before.\n\n## Measured\n\nEditor PlayMode, `benchmarks.yml`, medians in ms; the same instrumented tree with and without this change on the same runner class (the two before columns are two runs on it):\n\n| Case | Before | Before | After |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|\n| Clear 1k | 1558 | 1555 | 198 |\n| Replace 1k | 1741 | 1726 | 735 |\n| Create 1k | 627 | 627 | 657 |\n| Select / Swap / Remove one | 21 / 26 / 23 | 20 / 24 / 23 | 22 / 25 / 21 |\n\nClear stages, before to after: `StyleFlexMinSizeManipulator` removal 980 to 7 ms, the six click-gate unregistrations about 330 to 0 ms, the rest of the teardown about 250 to 190 ms.\n\nCreate is slightly slower in the same run (627 to 657, 221k to 242k GC.Alloc blocks): with the callbacks left registered, Unity's per-event record pools stay empty, so the next create allocates its callback records (21 per row) instead of reusing the ones a clear returned. Create has no single dominant stage: Button and Label construction is 19% of it, the per-element class, variant and layout passes most of the rest, and none of those is changed here. The 208 to 348 ms difference seen between runs is runner variance: one commit measured 398 and 223 ms on two runners, while repeats on one runner class agree within 1%.\n\nDocumentation: no guide describes teardown order, so no `Documentation~` change.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Tests pass locally (EditMode / PlayMode / generator tests as applicable): the generator suite (545) and the repository's duplication, refusal, tuple and assume-gate checks ran locally; this environment has no Unity editor, so both Unity suites run in CI.\n- [ ] New regression tests were verified red without the change and green with it: left to `Test / base-red` and `Test / unity-tests`; the two cases that count click-gate and text-item records fail on the base by construction, the rest are declared characterization.\n- [x] Docs are updated for every fact this change touches (guides, READMEs, CLAUDE.md) — or this PR has no doc impact: no doc impact.\n- [x] CHANGELOG fragment added for behavior/perf changes, named for the branch with `/` as `-`\n- [x] Known gaps or deliberate deferrals discovered here are filed as issues with acceptance criteria: none filed.\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01FoK7YxdRjMGmfmRkEEmS88\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
