          "distinct": true,
          "id": "5a6bd01b8c9c3fd270551c2ff11f93904aeb324f",
          "message": "perf(velvet): keep a pooled Button's click gate registered and skip the create-time text effect pass for a leaf with no effect (#1499)\n\n## What & why\n\nBuilds on #1498, which is merged; this branch carries main merged in.\n\n- A pooled Button's teardown unregistered its six click-gate callbacks, and UI Toolkit charges an unregistration more the more elements were created before it. The gate now stays registered on a pooled Button with its press state scrubbed, and the next rent adopts it instead of registering six callbacks again. A Button that does not go back to the pool, or lies below a discarded root, behaves as before.\n- Creating an element that carries no text-effect class no longer runs the text-effect pass: a detached, freshly created element has empty side tables and nothing to resolve.\n- Adds a benchmark for a list whose rows are pooled click-handling Buttons, the shape the keyed benchmark rows (plain containers, discarded rather than pooled) never reach.\n\n## Measured\n\nEditor PlayMode, `benchmarks.yml` dispatched on scratch branches (this change merged with the keyed benchmarks and the per-stage instrumentation, against the same without it), medians in ms. Runner classes differ between runs by up to 1.6x, so only the pair that landed on one class is read as a delta.\n\n| | before | after |\n|---|---|---|\n| Clear 1000 pooled-Button rows | 165.4 | 70.3 |\n| Clear 1000 pooled-Button rows, second pair (other runner class, after on the slower one) | 68.5 | 41.1 |\n| `StyleTextEffectResolver.Apply` in Create 1000 rows | 18.15 | 0.02 |\n| same, second pair | 5.39 | 0.01 |\n| Create 1000 rows (whole op) | 672.3 | 625.6 |\n\nWhole-op numbers move with the runner: untouched ops such as Select and Swap moved by the same ratio in that pair, so the per-stage rows are the evidence for the create change.\n\nExamined and left alone, with the reason:\n\n- `CornerRadiusFit.Observe` stays: its own remarks give the elements it exists for as those whose radius comes from a stylesheet rule or code, which no class names, so nothing on the element says it is not needed.\n- `new SkewPickElement` is the engine's `VisualElement` constructor; nothing extra is allocated for the subclass.\n- `ApplyResolvedLayoutManipulators` already early-outs per family; what remains is the text-item manipulator every Label and Button takes, which measures text whatever its classes.\n- Pool cap 32 to 1024 on Button and Label: Create fell but untouched stages such as `new SkewPickElement` fell by the same 20% in that pair, and clearing 1000 pooled Buttons got slower (52 to 90), so the evidence does not support a change.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Tests pass locally (EditMode / PlayMode / generator tests as applicable): generator suite 545 passed; the Unity suites run in CI\n- [ ] New regression tests were verified red without the change and green with it: the base-red check reads the pooled-row cases red; the text-effect cases are declared characterization\n- [x] Docs are updated for every fact this change touches (guides, READMEs, CLAUDE.md) — or this PR has no doc impact (no guide describes either mechanism)\n- [x] CHANGELOG fragment added for behavior/perf changes, named for the branch with `/` as `-`\n- [x] Known gaps or deliberate deferrals discovered here are filed as issues with acceptance criteria: not filed; the pooled-Button reset replaces the `Clickable`, which unregisters its five callbacks and registers five new ones per pooled Button\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01FoK7YxdRjMGmfmRkEEmS88\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
