          "distinct": true,
          "id": "3469aea6e971cd6bcf7ecce9b9a160c7a863b5f4",
          "message": "test(velvet): benchmark the js-framework-benchmark keyed operations (#1489)\n\n## What & why\n\nAdds `JsFrameworkKeyedBenchmarks` (PlayMode, `Velvet.Tests.Performance`), a port of the keyed operation set of the js-framework-benchmark suite, so a Velvet number can be read beside the same operation in the published React results. `KeyedBenchmarkApp` is the application: `Hooks.UseReducer` over the rows and the selected id, a `V.List` keyed by id, and a `[Component(Memoize = true)]` row whose callbacks are `UseCallback`-stable.\n\nOperations: create 1,000 rows, replace all 1,000, partial update (every tenth label), select, swap indices 1 and 998, remove one row, create 10,000, append 1,000 to 1,000, clear 1,000.\n\nEach case times one dispatch plus the synchronous scheduler flush that commits it, with the arrangement outside the window, and records GC.Alloc sample blocks from the recorder. There is no layout pass, as in `ReconcilerBenchmarks`. Counts come from `BenchmarkRun`, and one extra unmeasured iteration follows the loops. After every iteration the mounted buttons are compared with the state in order, and the number of row renders with what the operation should cause (select 2, swap 0, remove 0, partial update 100, append 1,000), so a case that misses the memoized path throws. `benchmarks.yml` already filters on `Velvet.Tests.Performance` and `benchmark_results.py` reads any Performance Testing result, so neither changed.\n\nNo comparison result is claimed. CI has not run this yet and no editor was available while writing it, so the first PlayMode run is the first compile and execution.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [ ] Tests pass locally (EditMode / PlayMode / generator tests as applicable) — not run locally; no editor here, CI is the first run\n- [x] New regression tests were verified red without the change and green with it — not applicable: benchmarks assert nothing about numbers; each is declared `GREEN_ON_BASE(characterization)`\n- [x] Docs are updated for every fact this change touches — `CONTRIBUTING.md` Benchmarks section lists the operations and where the port departs from the suite\n- [x] CHANGELOG fragment — none: contributor tooling, no user-visible behaviour\n- [x] Known gaps or deliberate deferrals discovered here are filed as issues with acceptance criteria — none found\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01FoK7YxdRjMGmfmRkEEmS88)_",
