          "id": "d254e78c669c0a5be51c730490caeb79f4a60725",
          "message": "fix(velvet): retry a newly mounted Portal whose content suspended with no boundary (#1500)\n\n## What & why\n\nA host whose update newly mounts `V.Portal(V.Component(Lazy))`, where `Lazy` reads a pending resource with no `V.Suspense` above, suspends in the drain of the Portals the pass mounted. That drain runs after the walk, so the placeholder and the rest of the render's rows were already in the container while the owner's `PreviousTree` stayed the older tree. The retry diffed from that older tree, built a second placeholder, and mounted a second `Lazy` under it; the registry keys a Portal's children by their placeholder, so that one started its resource again and suspended again. The Portal stayed empty and the host's effect never ran.\n\n- `ChildReconciler.DrainPendingPortalMounts` catches a suspend per entry, takes back rows a flat host run inserted ahead of the child that threw, records the Portal with `PortalSlotInfo.ChildrenPending`, keeps draining the entries behind it (the clear after the old escape lost them), and returns whether one suspended.\n- `Reconciler.FinishTopLevelPass` ends the pass with `FiberSuspendSignal.AfterTheWalk` once the rest of its work has run, or `Instance` where the walk itself threw.\n- `FiberRenderer.RenderAndReconcile` reads that identity: the owner keeps the tree its walk committed, drops its cached output and retires the old tree; the journal still abandons its hooks and effects, so the retry runs the effect whose deps changed once.\n- `FiberNodePatcher.PatchPortalChildren` diffs a pending Portal's children from nothing and clears the flag once they have mounted.\n- A suspend reached through `FiberCommitWork.DrainPendingWork` resumes a pass whose owner already holds that pass's tree, and the new render has not walked, so the owner is not given the new tree there; the pending record is what makes its retry consistent.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [ ] Tests pass locally (EditMode / PlayMode / generator tests as applicable) — generator suite 545/545 and the tuple, assume-gate, duplication and refusal censuses pass; no Unity editor was available, so EditMode and PlayMode are left to CI\n- [ ] New regression tests were verified red without the change and green with it — traced against the merge base, not run; `Test ▸ base-red` shows them\n- [x] Docs are updated for every fact this change touches (guides, READMEs, CLAUDE.md) — `react-migration.md` Suspense section\n- [x] CHANGELOG fragment added for behavior/perf changes, named for the branch with `/` as `-` — `Changelog~/unreleased/claude-portal-drain-suspend-retry.md`\n- [ ] Known gaps or deliberate deferrals discovered here are filed as issues with acceptance criteria — none filed\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01FoK7YxdRjMGmfmRkEEmS88)_",
