          "distinct": true,
          "id": "468d24f460b47d263f7139a6c2dd98d2aabb3f2f",
          "message": "perf(velvet): keep a pooled Button's Clickable and scrub its state in place (#1501)\n\n## What & why\n\n`ResetButtonForReuse` swapped the pooled Button's `Clickable`, costing about five `UnregisterCallback`/`RegisterCallback` calls per reuse, and `UnregisterCallback` cost grows with the number of elements that exist. The reset now keeps the Clickable and nulls its `clicked` / `clickedWithEventInfo` backing fields and clears its `active` state in place. If Unity's Clickable no longer exposes those members, it falls back to the old swap, so a handler cannot ghost either way. Not run or measured (no Unity available).\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [ ] Tests pass locally (EditMode / PlayMode / generator tests as applicable) -- not run, no Unity here\n- [ ] New regression tests were verified red without the change and green with it -- not verified\n- [x] Docs are updated for every fact this change touches -- no doc impact\n- [x] CHANGELOG fragment added\n- [x] No known gaps deferred\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01FoK7YxdRjMGmfmRkEEmS88)_",
