          "distinct": true,
          "id": "f238e524cad35c621ba00bc12b10710f2b64bb7d",
          "message": "fix(velvet): release the fibers of a suspended mount no Suspense caught (#1502)\n\n## What & why\n\nA component that suspends with no `V.Suspense` above it, inside a host element the retry creates again (a `V.Div` child of a `V.Portal`), left its fiber registered in `ComponentRegistry` on every attempt, since the retry mounts under a new element and so a new registry key. Hook subscriptions it made at render stayed until the root unmounted.\n\n`ReconcileChildrenOfNewElement` now handles a suspend raised with no Suspense primary open on the walk (the pass is abandoned): the fibers mounted under the element other than the reader and its ancestors are disposed at once. The reader and its ancestors stay, because the reader's resolve is what asks the host to retry (`NotifyAsyncResourceCompleted` ignores a disposed fiber); they are disposed right after `RetrySuspendedPasses` in the no-boundary branch. A suspend under an open primary is untouched, which `ElementCreationFailureTests` holds.\n\nNew case: `Given_APortalWhoseChildSuspendsInAHostElementItCreates_When_TheFirstResourceResolvesAndTheRetrySuspendsAgain_Then_OnlyTheLatestAttemptsReaderIsRegistered`. Not run locally: no Unity here. Expected red on the base (two fibers mounted on `second-a` elements) and green with the change; CI base-red and unity-tests are the evidence. The chained-reader retry cases must stay green.\n\nNot covered: where a Suspense boundary above the host catches the signal from the Portal drain, the reader is flagged but not disposed (the boundary branch of `NotifyAsyncResourceCompleted` is unchanged).\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [ ] Tests pass locally (EditMode / PlayMode / generator tests as applicable) - not run, no Unity available\n- [ ] New regression tests were verified red without the change and green with it - left to CI base-red and unity-tests\n- [x] Docs are updated for every fact this change touches - no doc impact; no guide describes fiber registration on suspend\n- [x] CHANGELOG fragment added (`unreleased/claude-suspend-orphan-fiber-cleanup.md`)\n- [x] Known gaps are listed above\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01FoK7YxdRjMGmfmRkEEmS88)_",
