          "distinct": true,
          "id": "f59c018e3cdc4b90b14977101a0994084e8b5147",
          "message": "fix(velvet): keep the rows a parked pass placed when a mounted Portal's child suspends (#1504)\n\n## What & why\n\nA time-sliced update can park after placing some rows, with the Portal it queued still to be mounted by the drain that ends the pass. When that Portal's child suspends with no `V.Suspense` above it, the pass is abandoned after its walk, and `RetainWalkedTree` declined to keep the walked tree because the reconciler had pending work. The owner's `PreviousTree` stayed the older tree, the parked resume (run first by the retry) still placed the abandoned tree's remaining rows, and the retry then diffed the older tree against the new one and created every row again. `RetainWalkedTree` now retains a parked walk too; `ReturnOldTreeAfterReconcile` parks the baseline for the resume as it does when a pass completes its slice.\n\nThe other two cases from the follow-up list were read and need no change:\n\n- A reader inside a host element a discarded Portal mount created restarts its resource on retry. That matches React, where the work of a mount that suspended is thrown away and a promise made inside the render is made again; the resource is cached by the caller, which `Hooks.Use` allows through a resource the caller owns (the `StableReaderRender` fixture in `SuspendWithoutBoundaryTests` reads one).\n- Several Portals suspending in one pass: the drain records each pending Portal separately, orders empty ranges that start at the same slot by tree position (`PortalSlotTracker.IsBehind`), and throws one signal at the end. Which reader the pass waits on only decides which resolve retries it, and a read still pending re-suspends the retry.\n\nNot changed, found while reading: the resumed-slice sibling in `FiberWorkLoop.ContinueReconcile` retires the parked baseline in its catch even when the slice parked again and then suspended in the drain, which leaves the parked state reading a retired tree. No case reaches it that I could build without running the editor.\n\nNo Unity editor was available, so nothing here was run. The new case was traced, not measured: on the merge base the retry should end with the host holding the rows twice, and with the change once. `Test ▸ base-red` and `Test ▸ unity-tests` are what show it.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [ ] Tests pass locally (EditMode / PlayMode / generator tests as applicable) — not run, no editor available; left to CI\n- [ ] New regression tests were verified red without the change and green with it — traced, not run; `Test ▸ base-red` shows it\n- [x] Docs are updated for every fact this change touches (guides, READMEs, CLAUDE.md) — `react-migration.md` Suspense section\n- [x] CHANGELOG fragment added for behavior/perf changes, named for the branch with `/` as `-` — `Changelog~/unreleased/claude-portal-suspend-edge-cases.md`\n- [ ] Known gaps or deliberate deferrals discovered here are filed as issues with acceptance criteria — none filed\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01FoK7YxdRjMGmfmRkEEmS88)_",
