          "distinct": true,
          "id": "8ab6f096a3e6ed1edda5f2c2cb1f9aff9add29c3",
          "message": "fix(velvet): leave a plain component below a bailed memo row alone when its sibling is dirty (#1503)\n\n## What & why\n\nA bailed memoized component's committed output is expanded on every parent re-render, and a component that is not memoized re-rendered whenever the expansion reached it. So any plain component in that output re-rendered on every parent tick: the row's root child, and the children of a fragment, Provider, Suspense or Memo, as in `[Component(Memoize = true)] Row(int id) => V.Component(Inner)`. When a component below the row also had an update pending, the row's element patch was kept (`GeneralPathReconciler.HoldsDirtyFiberBelow`) and re-rendered the plain components below that element too.\n\nInside the committed output of an inline fiber that rendered nothing in the pass, a non-memoized component whose node is the instance it last rendered from now bails unless it has an update pending, which is React's element-identity bail (`ReconcilerContext.InBailedOutput`, written in `GeneralPathReconciler.ExpandComponentInline` for every component including an error boundary, read in `ComponentRegistry.ReconcileExistingFiber`). A component with a fresh node or an update pending renders. After the change `Inner` above never re-renders on a parent tick.\n\nDocumentation: `react-migration.md` states it under the `React.memo` row. CHANGELOG fragment added.\n\nNot run: Unity is unavailable where this was written, so no test, compile or red/green run has happened. CI has to show the first new case red on the merge base (sibling render count 2 against 1). No test covers the root-child case yet.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [ ] Tests pass locally (EditMode / PlayMode / generator tests as applicable) - not run, no Unity here\n- [ ] New regression tests were verified red without the change and green with it - left to `Test > base-red`\n- [x] Docs are updated for every fact this change touches (guides, READMEs, CLAUDE.md) - or this PR has no doc impact\n- [x] CHANGELOG fragment added for behavior/perf changes, named for the branch with `/` as `-`\n- [x] Known gaps or deliberate deferrals discovered here are filed as issues with acceptance criteria - none found\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01FoK7YxdRjMGmfmRkEEmS88\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
