          "distinct": true,
          "id": "27917e961e13ab5feb336ea02381e8f6fe675b1a",
          "message": "perf(velvet): cut the cost of creating 1k keyed rows (#1505)\n\nNo issue: performance work on the js-framework-benchmark Create 1k rows operation.\n\n## What & why\n\n`FiberNodePatcher.ApplyVariantManipulators` ran ten configure passes (state, conditional, container, relational, has-, structural, has-class, attribute, supports, custom-property) for every element created or patched. For an element whose classes carry no variant token and which holds no variant state, each pass scanned the class list, several allocated arrays or lists, and none changed anything. A per-stage profile of Create 1000 rows (temporary instrumentation, since reverted) put these passes at about 40 ms of the operation's stage time, with the passes' own stages gone in the profiled run that carried this change.\n\nAfter `RecordVariantGateSource`, the method now returns when no class contains `:`, `[`, `(` or `_` (every variant token has a `:` prefix, and a custom-property token has a leading `[`, a `(` or a `_`) and the element is in none of the ten tables the passes write. An element that already holds variant state is still visited, so a re-render that drops its last variant removes the manipulator as before; a new case pins that.\n\n## Measured\n\nBenchmarks workflow, Create_1000Rows median in ms, single runs. Only runs on the same CPU are compared.\n\n| Runner CPU | main | this branch (head 7c40ef0a) |\n|---|---|---|\n| AMD EPYC 7763 | 545.6 | 505.5 |\n| AMD EPYC 9V45 | 192.5 | 171.4 (an earlier head that differs only in test text) |\n\nOther operations on the EPYC 7763 pair, main then branch: Clear 94.1 / 91.9, Replace 644.2 / 606.4, Select 19.3 / 19.7, Swap 22.4 / 23.1. Select and Swap do not take the changed path and move by less than the run-to-run noise (on the 9V45 pair Select read 10.7 against 17.8), so the Create delta is read as a direction, about 7 to 11 percent, not a precise figure.\n\nExamined and left alone: the Button constructor (82 ms), the six click-gate callbacks per Button (32 ms) and the flex-min text manipulator registration (26 ms) are UI Toolkit `RegisterCallback` costs that deferral would only move; `ChildReconciler.ReconcileUnder` (66 ms exclusive) was not split further.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [ ] Tests pass locally (EditMode / PlayMode / generator tests as applicable) -- no Unity here; the suites run in CI\n- [ ] New regression tests were verified red without the change and green with it -- the new case is declared `GREEN_ON_BASE(refactor)`: the base already removes the manipulator, and the case reddens only if the table check in the early return is cut; that cut was not run\n- [x] Docs are updated for every fact this change touches -- no guide describes this pass, no doc impact\n- [x] CHANGELOG fragment added for behavior/perf changes, named for the branch with `/` as `-`\n- [x] Known gaps or deliberate deferrals discovered here are filed as issues with acceptance criteria -- none filed; the unsplit `ReconcileUnder` cost is listed above\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01FoK7YxdRjMGmfmRkEEmS88\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
