          "distinct": true,
          "id": "c04088864951738699aa1bb62040370126d3a706",
          "message": "test(velvet): pin the parked-pass resume and the boundary path of a suspended mount, and fix a leak found there (#1508)\n\n## What & why\n\nTwo merged fixes had no regression test for the behaviour they protect.\n\n**Parked-pass resume.** A transition's time-sliced pass that parks and then suspends in a Portal drain with no Suspense above it waits for the retry the resolve asks for. New fixture `ParkedTransitionPassSuspendTests` pins, for the first slice and for a later slice that parks again:\n- `isPending` stays lit while the pass is suspended and clears at the commit of the retry;\n- the host's effect and the effect of a component the pass mounted each run once, including when the scheduled resume fires while the pass is suspended.\n\nThese six cases pass on the merge base (`GREEN_ON_BASE(characterization)`).\n\n**Suspended mount under a Suspense, and a leak it exposed.** Cases added to `SuspendWithoutBoundaryTests` cover a Suspense above a host whose update mounts a Portal element with a suspending reader: fallback, then content, and one registered fiber each for the reader and the sibling mounted ahead of it, plus one registered reader where an error boundary sits between the Suspense and the reader. The registered-count cases were red on the base: the abandoned first attempt's reader and sibling stayed registered after the reveal (2 instead of 1), because `DiscardSuspendedMountUnder` skipped the discard whenever a boundary existed and the boundary branches of the resolve disposed nothing.\n\nFix: the discard now applies there as well. The components mounted beside the reader are disposed when the attempt is abandoned. The reader and the components above it stay until the reader's resolve, and `NotifyAsyncResourceCompleted` disposes them in its boundary branches: after the reader's render in the ordinary branch, and without rendering the reader in the error-boundary-between and hidden-primary branches. `DisposeAbandonedMount` skips an already-disposed fiber.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [ ] Tests pass locally (EditMode / PlayMode / generator tests as applicable) - not run, no Unity available; CI is the evidence\n- [x] New regression tests were verified red without the change and green with it - the registered-count cases were red on the base in CI's base-red step and green with the fix; the rest pin merged behaviour and are declared `GREEN_ON_BASE(characterization)`\n- [x] Docs are updated for every fact this change touches (guides, READMEs, CLAUDE.md) — or this PR has no doc impact: no doc impact\n- [x] CHANGELOG fragment added for behavior/perf changes, named for the branch with `/` as `-`\n- [ ] Known gaps or deliberate deferrals discovered here are filed as issues with acceptance criteria\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01FoK7YxdRjMGmfmRkEEmS88\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
