          "distinct": true,
          "id": "d8c9030569160822970ec8dda3580fb8eff3039d",
          "message": "test(velvet): answer the mutation survivors under Runtime/Component (#1539)\n\nNo issue: the 3.0.0 release gate refuses the survivors this answers.\n\nThe mutation record holds 35 survivors under `Runtime/Component/` that nothing answered, and the release gate refuses a release while any standing survivor is unanswered. This answers all 35:\n\n- 30 are killed by new EditMode cases (`ComponentFiberAsyncStashTests`, `ComponentFiberMemoInvalidationTests`, `ComponentRegistryTableTests`, `BailedOutputSourceNodeTests`, `DragOverlayHostTests`, `MemoizationReportAttributeTests`, `ParticleBlendMaterialsTests`, `SortableContextIdTests`). Each pins behaviour the base already has, so each carries `GREEN_ON_BASE(characterization)`; the mutation record is what shows them red.\n- `ComponentRegistry.cs`'s `reusedAsIs` literal on the inline path is declared `MUTANT_SURVIVES(equivalent)`: its two readers act only on leaves and child fibers committed before the pass, and a newly created inline fiber has neither.\n- Four survivors sat on code that changed nothing, and that code is removed: the previous-link clear in `CommitChildOrder` (the next loop writes every link), the `kept` set in `ComponentRegistry` (every member is flagged `MountDiscarded` on the next line), the `Count > 0` guard before a dispose of an empty list, and the `reusedAsIs = false` seed, now computed once before the inline/wrapper branch.\n\nNo user-visible behaviour changes, so there is no CHANGELOG fragment and no documentation impact.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
          "timestamp": "2026-11-10T12:00:49+09:00",
          "tree_id": "56c5fb76932a8e304fecef5fe8dcfe68563370a2",
