          "id": "f236a4947ffdacbab9156063e91c94ab39439018",
          "message": "perf(velvet): stop a mutate round trip allocating what no listener or resume reads (#1578)\n\nRefs #1574\n\n`UseMutationPlayModeBenchmarks.UseMutation_OneMutateRoundTrip` went 53 → 85–91 blocks with the `MutationCache` (#1530); the benchmark history has no point between 0f643927 and ee23f5ce, so the attribution is read from the code. What a round trip allocated that no listener or resume reads:\n\n- **Cache events with no listener.** `MutationCache` built a `MutationCacheEvent` on every observer add/remove, announce, build, remove and clear — five per round trip. It now builds one only when `CacheListeners.HasListeners`.\n- **An eager settling source.** Every `Mutation` created its `Settled` completion source (four objects); only `ResumePausedMutations` waits on it. It is created on demand in `Continue`, and `SettleFunction()` completes it or flags the settle for a later ask.\n- **A success-path async helper.** `Hooks.DeliverSuccess` was its own async method (a state machine per success in a Debug build); its callbacks are inline in `RunMutationAsync` again, in v5's order.\n- **An options effect per render.** `Hooks.ObserveMutation` queued its passive effect whenever the caller passed a new record, about 15 allocations of passive-drain bookkeeping each; for a record equal to the committed one the effect would announce and reset nothing, so it is skipped. `MutationObserver.Options` and a pending `Mutation.Options` then keep the earlier, equal record.\n\nWhat remains — about 9 per round trip — is what v5 needs: the `Mutation` and its observer list, two states with the boxed variables and data, the function context, and the `UseContext` dependency.\n\nAlso fixed: `MutationCache.ResumePausedMutations` read `IsPaused` while continuing, so a paused call a scope continued inside an earlier one's `Continue` was skipped and the resume task didn't wait for its function; it now takes the paused set first, as v5's `filter` + `Promise.all` does.\n\nTests: `MutationAllocationTests` (no-listener events, the mutation's own allocations, an equal record costing what the committed one does) red on the base; `MutationObserverParityTests` cases for the resume settling, declared characterizations, and the scope-chained resume, red on the base. Labelled `benchmarks`.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
